00:04:46,666 --> 00:04:52,666
They Take War To A New Dimension.

2
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:39,333
Zone Troopers is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by Danny Bilson.

3
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:26,000
American soldiers, led by The Sarge, are stuck behind Nazi enemy lines.

4
00:19:06,666 --> 00:19:12,666
As they make their way across the Italian countryside, they come across
an alien spaceship that has crash-landed in the woods.

5
00:23:53,333 --> 00:23:59,333
The alien pilot is dead, but one of the ship's passengers is on the loose.

6
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
As the GIs hunt down the alien by splitting into smaller groups, they're not only tracked by the
Nazis, but also a whole host of other aliens come to save their stranded party.

7
00:33:26,666 --> 00:33:32,666
The Sarge, played by Tim Thomerson.

8
00:38:13,333 --> 00:38:19,333
Joey, played by Tim Van Patten.

9
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Mittens, played by Art LaFleur.

10
00:47:46,666 --> 00:47:52,666
Dolan, played by Biff Manard.

11
00:52:33,333 --> 00:52:39,333
The Alien, played by William Paulson.

12
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
Col. Manheim, played by Peter Boom.

13
01:02:06,666 --> 01:02:12,666
Zone Troopers is a 1985 American World War II science fiction film
directed by Danny Bilson and starring Tim Thomerson.

14
01:06:53,333 --> 01:06:59,333
It was filmed in Italy by Empire Pictures with
Charles Band as executive producer.

15
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
The original music score was composed by Richard Band.

16
01:16:26,666 --> 01:16:32,666
The film explores themes of spacecraft, nazi, italy, world war ii, hand grenade.

17
01:21:13,333 --> 01:21:19,333
The tone is thought_provoking.
